<title>AUSTRALIA: Pioneer reiterates 96/97 profit outlook.</title>
<headline>Pioneer reiterates 96/97 profit outlook.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Building materials group Pioneer International Ltd said on Thursday it still expects profit for the year to June 30, 1997 to be slightly lower than the 1995/96 profit.  </p>
<p>&quot;Nothing has changed, we still stand by what we said at the half year stage,&quot; Pioneer chief executive officer John Schubert told reporters after giving a speech to an Australia-Israeil Chamber of Commerce luncheon.</p>
<p>Pioneer said in February with the release of its results for the six months to December 31, 1996 that it expected its net profit for the full 1996/97 year to be materially lower than the previous year.</p>
<p>The Sydney-based group reported a net profit of A$258.3 million for 1995/96.</p>
<p>-- Kevin Morrison, Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1813</p>
